WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Hong Kong is steep.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:06.310
Its undulating terrain makes
rainwater hard to collect and store.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.250
Its own reservoirs supply only 20
to 30 per cent of the water it uses.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:18.030
Yet since 1982, its supply has run
24 hours a day, without interruption.

5
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.270
So where does the rest come from?

6
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.270
Huge underground aquifers?

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.190
Rationing?

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.930
In this mission, you'll see how a
growing city builds infrastructure,

9
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.010
from cleaning Victoria
Harbour to a rail-based city.

10
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll go under London, where a 25
kilometre super sewer was built to catch

11
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.110
storm overflows before
they reach the Thames.

12
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: explain how Hong
Kong has water 24 hours a day.
